5BSD no longer builds or boots a native 32-bit ARM kernel.

This directory remains for drivers shared with arm64. The native kernel
configuration, entry/exception/MMU/scheduler-switch code and release
profiles are retired. Do not remove this directory wholesale: arm64 still
uses its GIC, timer, PMU, and SoC drivers.
The ARM32-only QEMU, Qualcomm, Rockchip and TI platform trees were removed;
arm64 platform drivers live in `sys/arm64`, `sys/dev`, and the shared paths
here.
